  "term": "Nelson–Denny Reading Test",
  "definition": "The Nelson–Denny Reading Test is a standardized reading ability measure that includes a reading comprehension subtest. In the cited study, its comprehension score was more closely related than the WIAT-II comprehension subtest to how skilled adult readers adjusted their reading patterns when comprehension demands changed, suggesting it taps different aspects of comprehension than some other tests with the same label.",
